From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:14:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 279/404] Unified: the parts shelf on the tool strip, in Other
 tools and the design check
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- "Parts Shelf" next to "Put Part" on the tool strip (and on the Parts toolbar of the
  classic chrome); the Fasteners workbench under "Other tools"
- the tool search remembers what was typed, so that the shelf opens with "M6×20" found
- the design check takes a shelf screw in its tapped hole for the thread it is (the overlap
  is at most the ring between thread and tap drill), and does not list the shelf's hidden
  originals as hidden parts
- Japanese texts of the shelf

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
